{"qid":"Q491106","names":["Khanate of Khiva"],"title":"Khanate of Khiva","endonym":{"native":"دولت خورزم","lang":"fa"},"capsule":"The Khanate of Khiva was an Uzbek Turkic state in the Khorezm region of Central Asia, founded in 1511 when the Arabshahid dynasty's Ilbars Khan expelled the Persian garrison and established rule centered on the lower Amu Darya south of the Aral Sea. At its height it controlled the irrigated oasis towns of Khorezm and commanded caravan routes between Persia, the steppe, and Bukhara; three successive dynasties — Arabshahid, Tore, and Qungrat — ruled across four centuries of intermittent warfare with Persia, Bukhara, and nomadic neighbors. Russian General von Kaufman captured Khiva on 10 June 1873 after a three-column advance with 13,000 troops, and the treaty of 12 August 1873 reduced the khanate to a Russian protectorate, forcing emancipation of all slaves. The last khan abdicated on 2 February 1920 and the territory became the Khorezm People's Soviet Republic.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Territory is moderately well-attested for the core Khorezm oasis zone based on administrative and Russian survey records from the 19th century; outer nomadic tributary zones are poorly bounded and reconstructed conjecturally for earlier centuries.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Khanate of Khiva","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Khanate-of-Khiva"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Khanate of Khiva","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khanate_of_Khiva"}],"britannica":"place/khanate-of-Khiva","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Khanate of Khiva","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Ilbars I","